Grey and Grey Studio
====================

Grey is a text-to-speech model; Grey Studio is its desktop app. Both are made in the Netherlands by the people behind
thisvoiceisai.com. Contact: support@thisvoiceisai.com


1. Free for non-commercial use
------------------------------
Grey's code (this repository), the Grey models and Grey Studio are free for personal, non-commercial use: making speech for yourself, your own
projects and videos that aren't sold or paid for, research and learning. Commercial use (selling the speech, using it
in a paid product or service, or in advertising) is not allowed. Part of the speech data Grey learned from (the Emilia
dataset, CC BY-NC 4.0) and some of the voices only allow non-commercial use, so the models are licensed the same way.
You may change the code and share your changes under these same terms. You may not sell the code, Grey Studio or
the models, or offer them as a paid service.


2. Speech made with Grey is AI-generated: say so
------------------------------------------------
Everything Grey Studio and grey.py save is marked as AI-generated in two ways (dacts/marking.py), as the EU AI Act (Regulation (EU) 2024/1689,
article 50) asks of AI systems that make synthetic audio: a label inside the audio file, and an inaudible watermark in
the sound itself. Don't remove or hide them, and keep them in software you build on this code.
If you publish or share speech made with Grey, make clear it is AI-generated. That is your duty under the same law
(article 50(4)) when the speech could be taken for a real person, and it is always the fair thing to do. Never pass
Grey's speech off as a real recording.


3. Be fair with voices
----------------------
- A person's voice is personal data. Only clone or train voices that are your own, or that you have the speaker's
  permission for. For anyone under 16, a parent or guardian must agree.
- Don't use Grey to pretend to be a real person, to mislead people, to harass or defame anyone, for fraud, or for
  anything else that is against the law.
- Some built-in voices come with their own rules, which apply when you use them: Tsukuyomi-chan (© Rei Yumesaki) may
  not be used to criticise or attack people, to campaign for political or religious views, or for explicit content,
  and needs the credit "Grey:つくよみちゃん". The full list of credits and the speech data Grey learned from:
  https://thisvoiceisai.com/terms.html#credits (also: Grey Studio > Settings > Credits).
- Report misuse to support@thisvoiceisai.com.


4. Your privacy
---------------
Grey Studio works on your computer. Your text, your recordings, your voices, your takes and your trained models stay
on it: nothing of them is sent anywhere. Grey Studio only connects to thisvoiceisai.com to:
- check now and then whether a newer version exists, and download it (you can switch this off: Settings > Updates),
- download the voice models you choose on the Models page.
Those requests show thisvoiceisai.com and its network provider Cloudflare your IP address and the Grey Studio version
number, like any download does. Our server doesn't record them. There is no account, no tracking and no telemetry. More:
https://thisvoiceisai.com/privacy.html
If you make voices of other people, you are the one handling their personal data: ask for their permission and delete
their voice when they ask you to (Voices > the bin).


5. No warranty, liability
-------------------------
Grey Studio is free and provided "as is", without warranty: it may make mistakes, mispronounce words or stop working.
To the extent the law allows, we are not liable for damage caused by using it; this doesn't limit liability for intent
or gross negligence, or any rights you have as a consumer that can't be set aside. You are responsible for what you
make and publish with it.


6. Law
------
Dutch law applies to these terms. If you are a consumer, the mandatory protections of the country you live in still
apply to you.


7. Third-party software
-----------------------
Grey Studio includes Python (PSF License), PyTorch (BSD), Hugging Face Transformers (Apache 2.0), faster-whisper
(MIT) with OpenAI Whisper weights (MIT), XLM-RoBERTa (MIT), KVAE-Audio, WavLM (MIT), AudioSeal (MIT), the audEERING
emotion model (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0) and other open-source libraries, each under its own licence (see the licence files
inside python/Lib/site-packages).
